  "slug": "mirna-dysregulation-e0fb",
  "summary": "Recent preprints resolve cell-type-specific glial, metabolic and hypothalamic responses to amyloid and frontotemporal pathology.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is cell-type-resolved glial and metabolic responses accompanying amyloid and frontotemporal pathology. Two preprints place lysosomal programs at the centre of microglial reprogramming. A MiT/TFE lysosomal biogenesis program precedes and couples to disease-associated microglia (DAM) reprogramming across murine injury, amyloidosis and human AD. A GPNMB-marked, TREM2-dependent lysosomal state in FTD/AD mice is reversible and tracks neurodegeneration severity along the DAM continuum. Metabolic readouts extend this to astrocytes: human posterior cingulate proteomics and transcriptomics, combined with MRS and hyperpolarized pyruvate imaging in APP-KI mice, implicate glia in mitochondrial alterations. Single-nucleus profiling of 1.1 million hypothalamic nuclei in AD-BXD mice reveals sex-biased, cell-type-specific amyloid responses associated with early non-cognitive features. What is new is the temporal and sex-resolved framing of these glial responses. A separate study links diet-induced obesity to sex-dependent microvascular changes, with capillary loss and cognitive decline in males.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
